	(origin leaves a small bump at the start. So the pass begins at the)
	(definition's Begin Z, at whatever radius this level is cutting.)
	(Taken from _pl_begin_z, the definition's own Begin Z, rather than)
	(assuming 0.0 - the reference is wherever the operator put it. NOT from)
	(record 1 of the array: that is the first ITEM's endpoint, Z+1.0 here.)
	(Front-to-back only: with z_dir -1 the first segment is at the far end of)
	(the travel and this bound does not describe it. Untested there.)
	(THE TIP is what is bounded, not the cut. greatEndian: "when we are at)
	(0.0 Z and X at driven diameter we will be at cutting level already ..)
	(it is different now, we are reaching roughing diameter in the stock".)
	(The lead-in descends to the level radius at the tip's own start, so a)
	(tip bounded at Begin Z - nose arrives at the cutting diameter 0.4 mm)
	(INSIDE the stock, which is the thing being complained about. Bounding)
	(the cut instead was tried and is exactly wrong for that.)
	#<_org_z> = #<_pl_begin_z>
